\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Signed counts in one dimension}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{In one dimension the [grid simplices](fdip-013X) are the
oriented edges from #{r} to #{r+1}. An edge contributes #{1}
to the [signed count](fdip-013Y) at #{y} when it rises across
#{y}, and #{-1} when it falls across #{y}. A zero vertex
#{r} is nondegenerate exactly when both neighbors have nonzero
values. If #{f(r-1)<0<f(r+1)}, the edge leaving #{r} contributes
#{1} in a positive direction and the edge entering #{r}
contributes #{1} in a negative direction. Reversing both signs
gives local degree #{-1}. If the two neighbors have the same sign,
one direction sees two opposite contributions and the other
sees none. The local degree is then zero.}
